  "body": "Stacked on #817 (on #784, on #782). Review only the commit on top of #817's head 03437938. Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed (#637 E2c)\n- **`CarriedField::simulate(&mut self, ops) -> Result<(), StockError>`** lives in the new module `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field_carry_cut.rs`. It runs in four steps:\n  1. `check_ops` checks the moves as the caller stated them.\n  2. The first cut after a turn bakes the view's signed permutation into the bricks (`SdfField::turned`, E2a), so only the translation is left as the view.\n  3. Every move is shifted by that translation: `from`, `to`, and the arc centre in its plane's word order (`ArcPlane::words`). A translation keeps an arc's sense, plane and radius.\n  4. The moves are cut through `simulate_field`.\n- **`simulate_field`** is the field arm of `Stock::simulate`, moved word for word into a `pub(crate)` function in `backend.rs` so both callers share one tool construction (`spanning_flank`, batched per brick). Later cuts therefore ride the shipped +Z code: true XY arcs (#413) and the closed-form flat floor. On a flipped bake, the floor under the earlier cut is read by E2b's up-march from the moved `cut_downs`.\n- **The clip** is applied at read-back, as before. A cut and the clip block are both intersections, so the order does not matter. `column_body` still reads through `column_span`.\n- **`CarriedField` remembers a flip.** It gains a private, sticky `flipped` flag, set by `new` and OR-ed by `then`, with a `flipped()` accessor. `column_body` reads `floor_judged` from this flag instead of `turn.flips()`. Two reasons:\n  - After a flip is baked, the view is only a translation, and `turn.flips()` would forget that the floor has faced the spindle.\n  - Two flips composed by `then` make an upright turn, which also lost the flag before. The column engine's `Body::carry` keeps the flag sticky, so the field now agrees with it.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/781-field-simulate.md`: the lazy bake, the sticky flag, the refusal order, why `carry.rs` (394 lines) was left alone, and the zero-thickness tie.\n\n## Agreement results (`carry_engine_agreement`, both engines per column: `empty_at`, top and floor to 1e-6, `floor_judged`, volume)\n- **#780's three by-hand pins** now run through the real `simulate`, using one shared `chain_agrees` helper (carry, then cut, for any number of steps):\n  - cut after the flip;\n  - the slivers between a cut from below and one from above (`[2, 2.2]`, `[2.3, 2.6]`);\n  - the second slot through the first.\n- **`an_arc_cut_after_the_flip_carries_the_same_on_both_engines`** (new): half a circle about an off-lattice centre (10.1, 6.05), radius 3.7, flat r 1.3. It is cut from the new top at three depths:\n  - above the first slot's floor: 63 two-sided columns;\n  - into the sliver: 63 two-sided columns;\n  - through it: 63 empty columns.\n- **`a_second_carry_after_a_cut_carries_the_same_on_both_engines`** (new): flip, cut, then `then`, then cut again, at three depth pairs, in two chains:\n  - a quarter turn about Z;\n  - a flip back after an arc cut, so the bake moves the `cut_downs` records up again and the new `cut_ups` down.\n\n  Every chain reaches two-sided or empty columns (48 to 141 per chain), and both engines agree.\n- **The zero-thickness tie.** A third cut at exactly `5 - second` leaves a zero-thick column. The column engine's strict `top < floor` keeps it as material, while the field reads no material. That is a measure-zero tie, not a verdict. The fixture's depths sit off it, and the decision record says so.\n\n## Pins (`crates/sim/tests/field_carry.rs`)\n- **`simulate_cuts_what_the_bake_and_the_shifted_moves_cut_by_hand`** checks that `simulate` matches #780's by-hand path (bake, shift, `Stock::simulate`, translation-only view) bit for bit, through all 8 turns. The program has an XY arc and an XZ (G18) arc on a mesh plate. It compares distances and the whole `column_body` read-back.\n- **`a_refused_program_leaves_the_carried_stock_as_it_was`**: a NaN move or a negative radius is refused before the bake, and the view is unchanged.\n- **`a_flip_is_remembered_through_two_flips_and_a_bake`**.\n- **Mutation checks.** Each pin fails when its law is broken:\n  - Shifting an XZ arc's centre as if it were XY fails the by-hand pin.\n  - Dropping the centre shift fails the arc and second-carry agreement tests.\n  - Dropping the flip flag fails all 12 agreement tests.\n\n## Sweep through the verdict path (local, not committed; the round-3 review's approach)\n- **Fixture.** An 8 x 6 mesh plate at cell 0.5:\n  - floors {-6, -6.25, -6.1, -6.3, -5.9, -6.05, -6.2} and tops {0, 0.25, -0.2, 0.1, -0.05};\n  - a first slot from the top along y 3, r 2, at 10 depths from 0.5 under the floor to 3 above it (skins 0.01-0.3 among them);\n  - then a flip and a second slot from the new top along x 4, r 2, at 10 depths, both through `CarriedField::simulate`;\n  - flat and ball tools;\n  - 8 columns: under both slots, under one, beside them, and one off-lattice.\n- **Checks.**\n  - `Stock::top` and `column_span` against the exact interval.\n  - `Stock::deviate` against a part under the new floor, counting NaN columns where steel stands.\n- **Results.** **56000 reads, 56000 exact.**\n  - 0 under-read tops, 0 over-read floors.\n  - 0 NaN or refusal where steel stands.\n  - 0 `deviate` runs with a NaN column on material.\n  - Max over-read 4.5e-13.\n- **The off-lattice column (4.4, -2.6)** is judged at its cell's centre, which is how both engines sample a column. Judged at the point, a ball's curved floor differs by up to 0.025 there. The same difference shows upright on #817's head, and the round-3 review excluded it the same way (\"on-lattice\").\n\n## How tested (macOS, private `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`; debug unless noted)\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n| sim lib | 69 passed |\n| sim `carry_engine_agreement` | 12 passed |\n| sim `field_carry` | 12 passed |\n| sim `field_floor` / `field_skin` / `field_body` | 12 / 2 / 6 passed |\n| sim `stock_backend_parity` / `stock_sim` | 13 / 24 passed |\n| app `setup_carry` / `carried_verify` | 9 / 8 passed |\n| app `stock_engine_agreement`, release `--ignored` | 3 passed |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean |\n\nThe Linux quick gate (`--base 03437938`) follows in a comment.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No app holder calls `CarriedField::simulate` yet. Moving `Held`, `rest/across::sweep` and `PriorPlan` onto it is #586, which brings the app-level agreement lane.\n- Posed, rotary, cone and bull-nose ops after a carry go through the same `simulate_field`, so their tool construction is `Stock::simulate`'s. Only flat tools are fixtured after a carry: the sweep covers flat and ball, and the agreement suite flat.\n- A cylinder stock's clip is still refused by name on the field arm, as before.\n\nNo shipped verdict changes: the column engine is still the default, and `Stock::simulate`'s field arm is the same code moved into a function.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #781\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
